      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1897 the Yazoo Delta Railroad completed a depot named \"Doddsville\" after the Dodds brothers, linking the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doddsville%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1898 Doddsville boasted five stores and the Sunflower Lumber Company, a key player in the local timber industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doddsville%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historic landing called Standing Stump sat west of Doddsville on the Sunflower River, where boats from Vicksburg once docked during spring floods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
